feat(dietitian): spike-meal hover, annotations to patient, billing visibility, bigger meal photos

Closes the dietitian feedback loop: dietitians can now hover any CGM spike to see
the causal meal as a photo, click to annotate it, and the note flows directly to
the patient dashboard within seconds. Also surfaces billing intelligence on the
dietitian patient page (read-only) and significantly enlarges meal photos.

- New shared CgmMealChart with hover-to-pop-out causal meal photo
  + nearestMealForSpike engine helper (5 unit tests, 3h causal window)
- New MealAnnotationDrawer: hero photo, body, swap suggestion, send-to-patient
- New DietitianNotesCard on patient home with image, peak delta, recommendation,
  attribution, and Got-it acknowledge action
- Dietitian patient page: Billing tab (read-only banner + GpBillingCard variant),
  recent meals as full-width photo cards with status pills + Add-note CTA
- Meal queue right pane: 96x96 emoji thumbnail -> 288px hero photo with overlay
- Patient metrics CGM chart shows the same spike-meal callout with embedded
  Maya note when one exists
- patientStore gains MealAnnotation API (upsert/remove/acknowledge) with stable
  empty-array snapshots and per-key parse cache to satisfy React 19 strict
  useSyncExternalStore identity rules; useToastQueue snapshot stabilised too

201/201 tests pass, lint + build green.
